\caption(A counterexample to idempotence for signed, rather than magnitude-based, truncation. This behaviour is preserved from the original example.)
\alttext(A negative vector becomes a code with two negative values and two zeros after one gate, then becomes all zeros after a second gate.)

> The executed 101,200-parameter network

For d=784 and F=64, independent weights and biases contribute
\(2dF+F+d=101200\) learned scalars. The diagram executes a one-image shape probe with Graph
style and block detail. Named boundaries show the linear encoder, discrete rank selector,
two-input winner multiplication and sigmoid decoder. The selector dependency is declared
explicitly because host sorting creates a detached tensor; this does not add an autograd path
through the ranking. Shared linear shape scales, a two-pixel visibility floor and at most six
sampled feature-map planes and eight sampled vector units are explicit. Exact tensor shapes remain in labels and tooltips.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/k_sparse_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore p(1931);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& input) {
        const auto net = n::models::CompetitiveAutoencoder(p, input, false);
        n::model_stage("Linear encoder 784→64", input, net.raw);
        n::model_stage("Stable signed rank / top 8", net.raw, net.mask);
        n::model_stage(
            "Winner multiplication", std::vector<n::Tensor>{net.raw, net.mask}, net.code);
        return n::model_stage("Independent sigmoid decoder", net.code, net.reconstruction);
      },
      "k-sparse autoencoder: eight signed winners in 64 coordinates");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Graph;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.max_neurons = 8;
  options.sizing.spatial_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.channel_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 6;
  const auto figure             = model.plot(n::zeros({1, 784}), options);
  if (p.count() != 101200 || p.size() != 4 || figure.parameter_count() != 101200)
    return 1;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  figure.save_svg("build/k_sparse_architecture.svg");
  std::print(
      "{} learned tensors; {} learned scalars; selector is detached.\n", p.size(), p.count());
}
```
