4 learned tensors; 101200 learned scalars; selector is detached.
\image(figures/k_sparse_architecture.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The two gate inputs are preserved as separate graph dependencies. The mask is data derived from ranking, with no derivative assigned to its selection rule.)
\alttext(A branched executed graph follows the encoder into a selector and a direct activity path; both feed multiplication before an independent sigmoid decoder.)

> Genuine MNIST pools

The canonical dataset API prepares the same class-balanced, disjoint original-MNIST pools as
the earlier autoencoder reports: 1,000 fitting, 200 validation and 200 held-out images. Each is
Float32 [N,28,28,1] in [0,1], flattened only when entering a dense model. Official source IDs,
test labels and the provenance manifest are retained. Labels order the gallery only; they
never enter fitting or checkpoint selection.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", cache.string());
  const auto pools = n::models::LoadSaliency(cache / "saliency");
  n::save_npz(
      "build/k_sparse_data.npz",
      {{"fit_images", pools[0].images},
       {"validation_images", pools[1].images},
       {"test_images", pools[2].images},
       {"fit_source_ids", pools[0].source},
       {"validation_source_ids", pools[1].source},
       {"test_source_ids", pools[2].source},
       {"test_labels", pools[2].labels}});
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      cache / "saliency" / "manifest.json",
      "build/k_sparse_data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print("| pool | images | pixels per image | examples per digit |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i)
    std::print(
        "| {} | {} | 784 | {} |\n",
        i == 0   ? "fit"
        : i == 1 ? "validation"
                 : "test",
        pools[i].images.size(0),
        pools[i].images.size(0) / 10);
}
```
